window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-3a9100c321640450"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"deploy-the-windows-app-and-codex-cli\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"windows-codex-cli\">部署 Windows 应用和 Codex CLI</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可查看对应的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以将 Windows 桌面应用、Codex CLI，或两者同时部署到受管理的 Windows 设备。需要桌面访问时选择应用；需要终端访问时选择 CLI。</p> <p>桌面应用与独立 CLI 使用不同的安装上下文。部署 CLI 前，请先确定并验证用于运行安装程序的账户。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>目标</th> <th>从这里开始</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>分发桌面应用</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450?anchor=deploy-the-windows-app\">部署 Windows 应用</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>为员工提供独立的终端访问</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450?anchor=deploy-codex-cli-on-windows\">在 Windows 上部署 Codex CLI</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>在 Windows 上应用 Codex 管理要求</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450?anchor=configure-managed-requirements\">配置受管理的要求</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>准备 Windows 命令执行环境</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450?anchor=configure-the-windows-sandbox\">配置 Windows 沙箱</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"deploy-the-windows-app\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"windows\">部署 Windows 应用</h2> <p>请根据你使用的管理工具，以及设备能否访问 Microsoft 分发服务，选择合适的方法。</p> <p>部署前，请通过<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">受管理的配置</a>设置适用的控制项。如要在桌面应用中准备 Codex 命令执行环境，请按照 <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">Windows 沙箱设置</a>操作。检查设备兼容性，并完成任何必需的旧版环境设置。</p> <p>下面的 MSIX 链接会下载各处理器架构对应的最新版本，而不是历史版本。请检查下载的软件包，并将批准使用的安装包保存在部署系统中。请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-24c62848a3326493\">管理应用更新</a>协调应用内置更新程序与 Microsoft Store、Intune 及其他部署工具。</p> <p><a id=\"deploy-the-app-with-an-enterprise-management-tool\"></a></p> <p><strong>windows-deployment</strong></p> <p>安装包来源</p> <p><strong>windows-intune-source</strong></p> <p><a id=\"deploy-through-microsoft-store\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"microsoft-store\">通过 Microsoft Store 部署</h3> <p>使用 Intune 的 Microsoft Store 集成功能安装并更新应用。</p> <ol> <li> <p>在 Intune 管理中心中，依次打开 <strong>Apps</strong> &gt; <strong>All apps</strong> &gt; <strong>Create</strong>。选择 <strong>Microsoft Store app (new)</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>搜索来自 <strong>OpenAI</strong> 的 <strong>ChatGPT</strong>，或输入 Store 产品 ID <code>9PLM9XGG6VKS</code>。选择应用并检查其安装设置。</p> </li> <li> <p>在 <strong>App information</strong> 中，将 <strong>Install behavior</strong> 设为 <strong>System</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>在 <strong>Required</strong> 下添加目标组，让 Intune 自动安装应用，然后选择 <strong>Create</strong>。</p> </li> </ol> <p>如需通过 Company Portal 提供可选安装，请改用 <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong>。</p> <p>设备必须能够访问 Microsoft <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/fundamentals/endpoints#microsoft-store\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">网络要求（需联网）</a>中列出的 Microsoft Store 和 Windows Update 终结点。如果这些终结点被阻止，请选择 <strong>离线 MSIX</strong>。</p> <p>有关安装上下文、网络要求和部署监控，请参阅 Microsoft 的 <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-microsoft-store\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Intune Store 应用指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"deploy-an-offline-package-with-intune\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"intune\">使用 Intune 部署离线安装包</h3> <p>如果设备无法使用 Microsoft 分发服务，或者你需要分发组织已审核的软件包，请使用下载的 MSIX。链接会下载最新版本。重复部署时，请使用部署系统中已批准的安装包。要自动安装，请选择 <strong>Required</strong>。</p> <p>阻止访问 Microsoft Store 应用，并不会阻止 Intune 通过 Microsoft Store 集成功能部署应用。你仍可以使用<strong>推荐的 Microsoft Store</strong> 方式。</p> <p>分配方式</p> <p><strong>windows-intune-assignment</strong></p> <ol> <li> <p>为你的设备下载 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX（需联网）</a> 或 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX（需联网）</a>。</p> </li> <li> <p>在 Intune 管理中心中，依次打开 <strong>Apps</strong> &gt; <strong>All apps</strong> &gt; <strong>Create</strong>。 选择 <strong>Line-of-business app</strong>，上传 MSIX，并检查安装包信息。</p> </li> <li> <p>在 <strong>Assignments</strong> 中，将目标设备组添加到 <strong>Required</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>在该分配的 <strong>Install Context</strong> 列中选择 <strong>User context</strong>，将其更改为 <strong>Device context</strong>，然后保存。</p> </li> <li> <p>检查并创建应用。在 <strong>Device install status</strong> 中确认安装成功，然后让员工正常启动 ChatGPT。</p> </li> </ol> <p>如果应用没有显示，请让用户先注销再重新登录。</p> <p>更多信息请参阅 Microsoft 的 <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-lob-windows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">LOB 应用部署指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>如要通过 Company Portal 提供安装，请将离线安装包部署为 <strong>Windows app (Win32)</strong>，并将分配方式设为 <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong>：</p> <ol> <li> <p>下载 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX（需联网）</a> 或 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX（需联网）</a>，以及<a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-License.xml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">离线许可证（需联网）</a>。将安装包重命名为 <code>ChatGPT.msix</code>，并将两个文件保存在同一文件夹中。</p> </li> <li> <p>将此脚本保存为下载文件旁的 <code>Install-ChatGPT.ps1</code>：</p> </li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">   #Requires -RunAsAdministrator\n   $ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\n   Add-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online `\n     -PackagePath \"$PSScriptRoot\\ChatGPT.msix\" `\n     -LicensePath \"$PSScriptRoot\\ChatGPT-License.xml\" `\n     -Regions all\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>将此脚本保存为 MSIX、许可证和安装脚本旁边的 <code>Uninstall-ChatGPT.ps1</code>。配置 Intune 在卸载应用时以 System 上下文运行此脚本。该脚本会移除设备上所有用户的预配软件包和应用注册信息：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">   #Requires -RunAsAdministrator\n   $ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\n   Get-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online |\n     Where-Object DisplayName -eq 'OpenAI.Codex' |\n     Remove-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online -AllUsers\n\n   Get-AppxPackage -AllUsers -Name 'OpenAI.Codex' |\n     Remove-AppxPackage -AllUsers\n</code></pre> <p>两个脚本都应遵循组织的 PowerShell 脚本签名策略。</p> <ol> <li>使用 Microsoft 的 <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-win32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Win32 应用工作流（需联网）</a>，将 MSIX、许可证、<code>Install-ChatGPT.ps1</code> 和 <code>Uninstall-ChatGPT.ps1</code> 打包在一起。在 Intune 中添加 <strong>Windows app (Win32)</strong>，将 <strong>Install behavior</strong> 设为 <strong>System</strong>，并指定安装包对应的处理器架构。配置下面的 64 位安装和卸载命令，然后将应用分配为 <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong>。</li> </ol> <details> <summary>Win32 安装、卸载和检测设置</summary> 将 <strong>Install command</strong> 设为： <pre><code class=\"language-text\">%SystemRoot%\\Sysnative\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe -NoProfile -File .\\Install-ChatGPT.ps1\n</code></pre> 对于 Windows 安装在 <code>C:\\Windows</code> 的设备，将 <strong>Uninstall command</strong> 设为： <pre><code class=\"language-text\">C:\\Windows\\Sysnative\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe -NoProfile -File .\\Uninstall-ChatGPT.ps1\n</code></pre> 如果 Windows 安装目录不同，请使用实际路径。这个字面路径会在 Intune 的 32 位命令上下文中选择 64 位 Windows PowerShell。不要在卸载字段中替换为 <code>%SystemRoot%</code>：Intune 不会在该字段展开环境变量。如果需要展开变量，请按 Microsoft 的<a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-win32#step-2-program\">程序设置（需联网）</a>说明打包一个包装脚本。 请在 64 位 PowerShell 中运行此自定义检测脚本。当应用已在设备上预配时，脚本会报告成功。如需检测某个指定的批准版本，还应将软件包的 <code>Version</code> 与该版本进行比较。 <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$package = Get-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online -ErrorAction Stop |\n  Where-Object DisplayName -eq 'OpenAI.Codex'\n\nif ($package) {\n  Write-Output $package.PackageName\n  exit 0\n}\nexit 1\n</code></pre> Windows 会在用户登录时注册已预配的软件包。如果应用没有显示，请让用户先注销再重新登录。 </details> <p><a id=\"deploy-with-microsoft-configuration-manager-sccm\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"microsoft-configuration-manager-sccm\">使用 Microsoft Configuration Manager (SCCM) 部署</h3> <p>通过 Configuration Manager 和 Software Center 部署下载的 MSIX。</p> <ol> <li> <p>为你的设备下载 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX（需联网）</a> 或 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX（需联网）</a>。将其放在 Configuration Manager 可以访问的网络共享文件夹中。</p> </li> <li> <p>依次打开 <strong>Software Library</strong> &gt; <strong>Application Management</strong> &gt; <strong>Applications</strong> &gt; <strong>Create Application</strong>。选择 <strong>Windows app package</strong> 并输入 MSIX 路径。检查检测到的软件包信息，并启用 <strong>Provision this application for all users on the device</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>将内容分发到分发点，并部署到设备集合。选择 <strong>Required</strong> 以自动安装， 或选择 <strong>Available</strong> 让用户从 Software Center 安装。</p> </li> </ol> <p>请使用 Windows 应用软件包部署类型，而不是 Store 链接类型。有关软件包要求和为所有用户预配的说明，请参阅 Microsoft 的 <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/configmgr/apps/get-started/creating-windows-applications\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Configuration Manager 指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>如果部署工作流需要，请同时下载<a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-License.xml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">离线许可证（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"remove-a-provisioned-app-with-configuration-manager\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"configuration-manager\">使用 Configuration Manager 移除已预配的应用</h4> <p>如果用户已经在已预配此应用的设备上登录过，请创建以下两种卸载部署：</p> <ol> <li> <p>将一个卸载部署分配给包含受影响设备的<strong>设备集合</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>将第二个卸载部署分配给包含已在这些设备上登录过的用户的<strong>用户集合</strong>。</p> </li> </ol> <p>从设备中移除已预配应用，并不会为现有用户卸载该应用。请分别验证设备和这些用户账户中的卸载结果。请参阅 Microsoft 的<a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/configmgr/apps/get-started/creating-windows-applications#provision-windows-app-packages-for-all-users-on-a-device\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">移除已预配应用指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"deploy-with-another-management-tool\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_1\">使用其他管理工具部署</h3> <p>使用你的管理工具提供的 MSIX 部署工作流。</p> <ol> <li> <p>为你的设备下载 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX（需联网）</a> 或 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX（需联网）</a>。</p> </li> <li> <p>将 MSIX 添加到部署工具。使用 Local System 或管理员权限，配置设备级安装。</p> </li> <li> <p>将自动安装分配给试点设备组。在扩大部署范围前，确认员工能使用自己的常规 Windows 账户打开 ChatGPT。</p> </li> </ol> <p>如果应用没有显示，请让用户先注销再重新登录。</p> <details> <summary>使用 PowerShell 脚本安装</summary> 如果你的工具需要安装命令，请将<a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-License.xml\">离线许可证（需联网）</a>与 MSIX 一并下载。 将安装包重命名为 <code>ChatGPT.msix</code>，并将此脚本保存在同一目录下，命名为 <code>Install-ChatGPT.ps1</code>： <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">#Requires -RunAsAdministrator\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\nAdd-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online `\n  -PackagePath \"$PSScriptRoot\\ChatGPT.msix\" `\n  -LicensePath \"$PSScriptRoot\\ChatGPT-License.xml\" `\n  -Regions all\n</code></pre> 请将脚本和两个文件打包在一起。配置管理工具使用 64 位 Windows PowerShell，以 Local System 或管理员身份运行脚本。 </details> <p><a id=\"let-users-install-and-update-the-app\"></a></p> <p>安装包来源</p> <p><strong>windows-user-source</strong></p> <p><a id=\"let-users-install-the-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">让用户自行安装应用</h3> <p>当用户可以自行安装应用，或能向管理员寻求帮助时，请使用此选项。</p> <ol> <li> <p>请用户访问 <a href=\"https://get.microsoft.com/installer/download/9PLM9XGG6VKS?cid=website_cta_psi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Windows 安装程序（需联网）</a>。</p> </li> <li> <p>运行安装程序，并按照 Windows 安装提示操作。安装需要管理员批准。</p> </li> <li> <p>打开 ChatGPT，并使用工作账户登录。</p> </li> </ol> <p>用户也可以通过命令行安装：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">winget install --id 9PLM9XGG6VKS -s msstore\n</code></pre> <p>安装程序会自动更新。安装或更新期间可能会出现 Microsoft Store 组件；用户无需打开 Store。</p> <p><a id=\"install-without-microsoft-distribution-services\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"install-from-an-offline-package\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">从离线安装包安装</h3> <p>在可联网的电脑上下载文件，然后将它们复制到目标设备。安装必须由管理员执行。</p> <ol> <li> <p>下载 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX（需联网）</a> 或 <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX（需联网）</a>，以及<a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-License.xml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">离线许可证（需联网）</a>。将安装包重命名为 <code>ChatGPT.msix</code>，并将两个文件保存在同一文件夹中。</p> </li> <li> <p>以管理员身份在该文件夹中打开 Windows PowerShell 并运行：</p> </li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">   Add-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online `\n     -PackagePath .\\ChatGPT.msix `\n     -LicensePath .\\ChatGPT-License.xml `\n     -Regions all\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>如果应用没有显示，请先注销再重新登录，然后打开 ChatGPT 并使用工作账户登录。</li> </ol> <p>下载链接会提供各处理器架构对应的最新 Store 签名软件包。离线安装后，仍需联网才能使用 ChatGPT。桌面应用不提供独立 MSI 或非 Store 的 EXE 软件包。</p> <p><a id=\"deploy-codex-cli-on-windows\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"windows-codex-cli_1\">在 Windows 上部署 Codex CLI</h2> <p>准备 CLI 软件包、应用设备策略，并从员工账户验证终端访问。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">开始之前</h3> <ul> <li>确定目标 Windows 设备、用户和处理器架构，然后选择安装方法。确认用户有权使用 Codex，并能完成组织要求的登录流程。</li> <li>使用 Intune 时，请准备应用管理权限、符合 <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/create-win32-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microsoft Win32 打包前提条件（需联网）</a>的已注册设备，以及无人值守安装软件包。</li> <li>明确负责 CLI 更新和卸载的人员。如果使用 npm，请考虑受管理的 Node.js/npm 安装及其全局软件包位置。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"choose-an-installation-method\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">选择安装方法</h3> <p>选择安装方式和明确的 CLI 版本。查看 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub 上的 CLI 版本（需联网）</a>，然后在示例中将 <code>&lt;approved-version&gt;</code> 替换为经批准的 <code>x.y.z</code> 格式版本号。软件包与检测规则必须使用相同版本。</p> <p>如果没有指定版本，独立安装程序默认会安装 <code>latest</code>。请显式设置 <code>-Release</code>，将部署固定到某个版本；参数说明见<a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d/scripts/install/install.ps1#L1-L14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">安装程序的版本参数（需联网）</a>。常规安装说明请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">CLI 安装指南</a>。</p> <p><strong>独立 PowerShell 安装程序。</strong> 在新的 PowerShell 窗口中，下载安装程序并传入批准的版本：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$CodexRelease = '&lt;approved-version&gt;'\nInvoke-WebRequest -UseBasicParsing -Uri 'https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1' -OutFile '.\\codex-install.ps1'\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\codex-install.ps1 -Release $CodexRelease\n</code></pre> <p><strong>npm。</strong> 如果设备上已由管理员管理 Node.js 和 npm，请明确选择已批准的软件包版本：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$CodexRelease = '&lt;approved-version&gt;'\nnpm install -g \"@openai/codex@$CodexRelease\"\n</code></pre> <p>对于受管理的分发，请将已审核的安装程序或软件包以及选定版本保存在 IT 管理的软件包中。明确安装上下文、检测、卸载和更新方式。选择某个版本并不会更改安装程序的用户配置文件默认值，也不会提供完整的无人值守部署包装程序。</p> <p><a id=\"set-the-installation-context\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">设置安装上下文</h3> <p><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">独立安装程序（需联网）</a>默认会将运行时文件安装到当前用户的配置文件中，将命令目录设为 <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\OpenAI\\Codex\\bin</code>，并修改<strong>用户 PATH</strong>。</p> <p>以 <strong>SYSTEM</strong> 身份运行未修改的安装程序时，目标会变成 SYSTEM 配置文件和环境。在 Intune 中选择 <strong>System</strong>，并不会将其变成面向所有用户的安装。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>部署选择</th> <th>需要验证的内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>为当前登录员工安装</td> <td>在该员工的用户上下文中运行安装和检测。在新的终端中确认员工能够找到并运行 <code>codex</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>构建设备级软件包</td> <td>明确并验证机器级安装布局、运行时文件、权限、PATH 可见性、检测和卸载方式。默认安装程序不提供这种设计。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>使用 npm</td> <td>确认运行 npm 的账户所使用的全局软件包前缀和命令位置。“全局”并不一定代表适用于所有 Windows 用户。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>请将用户安装、设备策略下发和管理员批准的沙箱设置分开处理。流程要求使用员工配置文件时，应使用该员工的身份，而不是 SYSTEM。</p> <p>请将独立运行时文件放在一起；只复制 <code>codex.exe</code> 并不能构成完整的独立软件包。</p> <p><a id=\"package-and-assign-the-cli-through-intune\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"intune-cli\">通过 Intune 打包并分配 CLI</h3> <p>请为选定的安装上下文准备并验证一个由 IT 管理的 Win32 软件包，其中包含无人值守安装程序、卸载程序和检测逻辑。</p> <ol> <li> <p>准备源文件夹，放入已批准的安装负载和无人值守设置脚本。在脚本中指定批准的 CLI 版本，不要允许它解析为 <code>latest</code>。Microsoft 打包工具及其输出文件夹应放在该源文件夹之外。</p> </li> <li> <p>使用 Microsoft Win32 Content Prep Tool 生成 <code>.intunewin</code> 文件。此示例假定已审核的设置脚本名为 <code>Install-Codex.ps1</code>：</p> </li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">   IntuneWinAppUtil.exe -c C:\\Packages\\Codex\\Source -s Install-Codex.ps1 -o C:\\Packages\\Codex\\Output -q\n</code></pre> <p>该工具会打包源文件夹中的内容。请参阅<a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/create-win32-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">创建 Win32 应用软件包（需联网）</a>。</p> <ol> <li> <p>在 Intune 中创建 <strong>Windows app (Win32)</strong> 并上传软件包。</p> </li> <li> <p>按照软件包的设计，设置安装和卸载命令、<strong>User</strong> 或 <strong>System</strong> 行为、要求和检测规则。</p> </li> <li> <p>将其分配为 <strong>Required</strong> 或 <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong>。</p> </li> </ol> <p>Intune 要求使用无人值守安装。自定义检测脚本必须以代码 <code>0</code> 退出并向 stdout 写入内容；如果输出写入 stderr，检测会失败。请参阅<a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-win32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">添加并分配 Win32 应用（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>即使管理代理报告退出代码成功，也要使用员工账户验证 CLI。</p> <p>对于 Configuration Manager (SCCM)，请在应用程序工作流中使用已审核的 CLI 安装设计，并设置 CLI 专用的安装程序和检测规则。桌面应用的 MSIX 设置只适用于桌面应用。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-managed-requirements\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">配置受管理的要求</h3> <p>将管理员强制执行的 Windows 要求部署到：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">%ProgramData%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\requirements.toml\n</code></pre> <p>通过终端管理工具下发此文件。为目标用户提供读取权限，并阻止普通用户更改由管理员管理的策略。</p> <p>要求用于限制设置；配置默认值用于提供起始值。请检查本地文件和适用的云端策略，以确定最终生效的配置。</p> <p>请针对权限、审批、网络访问和沙箱行为设置要求。有关受支持字段及优先级，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=locations-and-precedence\">受管理的配置</a>。</p> <p>部署后，以员工身份启动 Codex，并使用 <code>/status</code> 和 <code>/debug-config</code> 确认生效的策略。安装 CLI 或下发要求，并不会自动授予工作区访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-the-windows-sandbox\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"windows_1\">配置 Windows 沙箱</h3> <p>选择 Windows 沙箱前，请检查设备兼容性。<a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">Windows 沙箱指南</a>介绍了 Microsoft Execution Containers (MXC) 和旧版实现。</p> <p><a id=\"prefer-mxc-on-compatible-devices\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"mxc\">在兼容设备上优先使用 MXC</h4> <p>对于独立 CLI，请在 <code>config.toml</code> 中启用 MXC 优先选项：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[features]\nprefer_mxc = true\n</code></pre> <p>你也可以通过 <code>requirements.toml</code> 强制设置此功能值。MXC 不可用时，此优先设置允许回退到旧版实现。启用前，请在 Windows 沙箱指南中检查设备要求。</p> <p>对于 CLI 0.162.0 或更高版本，请在项目目录中运行以下兼容性探测：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">codex -c windows.sandbox=mxc sandbox --include-managed-config --permission-profile :workspace -- cmd.exe /d /c echo MXC_OK\n$LASTEXITCODE\n</code></pre> <p>预期结果为 <code>MXC_OK</code>，退出代码为 <code>0</code>。此检查只验证显式调用 MXC 的命令；还应检查员工日常会话的配置。</p> <p>推出前，请将沙箱指南中的网络限制与受管理的网络策略进行比较。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-legacy-fallback\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_8\">准备旧版回退方案</h4> <p>如果 MXC 不可用或已禁用，请优先选择 <code>elevated</code> 旧版回退方式。此方式需要管理员批准设置，但沙箱中的命令会以非管理员权限运行。</p> <p>请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">由 IT 主导的设置流程</a>，针对员工账户和 Codex 主目录完成设置。从具有适当提升权限的进程中运行以下示例：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">codex sandbox setup --elevated --user 'DOMAIN\\alice' --codex-home 'C:\\Users\\alice\\.codex'\n</code></pre> <p>请将示例中的身份和路径替换为目标用户的实际值。进行提升权限设置时，请使用管理员信任的 CLI 安装。</p> <p>如果只允许提升权限的旧版实现，请将以下内容添加到 <code>%ProgramData%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\requirements.toml</code>，而不是 <code>config.toml</code>。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2?anchor=configure-a-legacy-fallback\">配置旧版回退</a>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[windows]\nallowed_sandbox_implementations = [\"elevated\"]\n</code></pre> <p>此设置会限制旧版回退，但不会阻止 MXC。在允许使用 <code>unelevated</code> 之前，请先评估其网络隔离较弱，且不支持拒绝读取路径的风险。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-cli-deployment\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"cli\">验证 CLI 部署</h3> <p>请以目标员工身份打开一个新的、非管理员 PowerShell 窗口：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">Get-Command codex\ncodex --version\ncodex\n</code></pre> <p>确认解析到的可执行文件来自预期安装位置，然后完成已批准的登录流程。在指定的测试项目中运行一个小任务，并检查当前生效的配置。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>检查项</th> <th>操作与预期结果</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>安装上下文</td> <td>确认 CLI 从目标员工账户中解析，包括重新登录后仍然如此。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>管理工具检测</td> <td>确认已安装 CLI 的设备会被检测到；未安装 CLI 的设备（包括已经卸载的设备）不会被检测到。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>受管理的要求</td> <td>确认会话显示预期的有效策略。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Windows 沙箱</td> <td>验证兼容设备上的 MXC 可正常工作，并在需要时配置获准的旧版回退方案。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>更新</td> <td>确认部署后员工可以运行已批准的新版本。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>卸载</td> <td>确认软件包能移除自身安装内容和 PATH 条目，但不会删除无关的用户配置或项目数据。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"manage-in-app-updates\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"manage-updates\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">管理更新</h2> <p><a id=\"desktop-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">桌面应用</h3> <p>默认情况下，应用会检查更新，包括离线安装的情况。要启用自动更新，请允许设备访问 <code>persistent.oaistatic.com</code>。如果禁用了自动更新，请通过管理工具部署较新的软件包。</p> <p>请按照<a href=\"#/article/a-24c62848a3326493\">管理应用更新</a>协调所有更新来源。禁用内置更新程序并不会阻止 Microsoft Store、Intune 或其他管理工具更新应用，也不会提供 OpenAI 管理的版本固定或独立发布通道。请通过部署系统确认已安装版本。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-cli\">Codex CLI</h3> <p>每次更新 CLI 时，都要选择新的批准版本，在部署软件包中更新明确指定的 <code>-Release</code> 值或 npm 软件包版本，并更新检测规则。通过软件包流程部署后，验证安装版本、账户上下文和检测行为。没有明确指定版本时，不要将受管理的软件包切换回安装程序命令。请参阅 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI 版本（需联网）</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">CLI 安装与更新</a>以及 <a href=\"https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/using-npm/package-spec\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">npm 版本选择（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">故障排查</h2> <details> <summary>安装时提示用户输入管理员凭据</summary> 用户自行安装应用时，必须由管理员批准。 通过 Microsoft Store 使用 Intune 部署时： 1. 在 Intune 管理中心中打开 <strong>Apps</strong> &gt; <strong>All apps</strong>，然后选择 ChatGPT。 2. 在应用的 <strong>Properties</strong> 中检查 <strong>Install behavior</strong>。如果当前值是 <strong>User</strong>，请将应用重新添加为 <strong>Microsoft Store app (new)</strong>，并在 <strong>App information</strong> 中选择 <strong>System</strong>。 3. 将应用分配到目标组的 <strong>Required</strong> 或 <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong>。如果添加了新应用，请移除原应用对该组的分配。 4. 使用 Intune 同步受影响的设备，然后检查 <strong>Device install status</strong>。 对于可选分配，请在 Company Portal 中重试安装。 如果应用已经安装，使用 <strong>System</strong> 安装行为进行部署可能导致 Intune 报告 <code>0x87D1041C</code>。在这种情况下，安装仍然成功。请在受影响的设备上验证应用。 </details> <details> <summary>安装失败，错误代码为 <code>0x80073D28</code></summary> 如果 Windows 无法在没有管理员权限的情况下安装打包服务，会返回 <code>0x80073D28</code>（<code>ERROR_PACKAGED_SERVICE_REQUIRES_ADMIN_PRIVILEGES</code>）。 请以管理员身份运行安装程序，或将部署工具配置为在设备或 System 上下文中安装。 对于现有的 SCCM 部署： 1. 打开应用的 <strong>Properties</strong> &gt; <strong>Deployment Types</strong>。 2. 编辑 <strong>Windows app package</strong> 部署类型，并打开 <strong>User Experience</strong>。 3. 启用 <strong>Provision this application for all users on the device</strong> 并保存。 4. 刷新客户端的计算机策略，然后在 Software Center 中重试安装。 有关预配设置的详情，请参阅 Microsoft 的<a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/configmgr/apps/deploy-use/create-applications#automatically-detect-application-information\">应用部署设置（需联网）</a>。 </details> <p><a id=\"codex-cli-installation-and-configuration\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-cli_1\">Codex CLI 安装与配置</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>症状</th> <th>检查事项</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Intune 报告成功，但员工无法运行 Codex</td> <td>检查安装账户、运行时位置，以及被更新 PATH 的账户。以 SYSTEM 身份运行未修改的安装程序，不会将 Codex 安装到员工配置文件中。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>安装后无法识别 <code>codex</code></td> <td>打开新的终端。检查目标账户的命令目录和 PATH。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>启动了错误的 Codex 版本</td> <td>使用 <code>Get-Command codex</code> 检查是否存在冲突的独立版或 npm 安装位置。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MXC 探测失败</td> <td>对照 Windows 沙箱指南，检查设备能力、CLI 版本和受管理策略。必要时预配获准的旧版回退方案。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>旧版沙箱设置要求管理员批准</td> <td>使用员工身份和 Codex 主目录完成由 IT 主导的设置。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>生效的受管理设置与本地 requirements 文件不同</td> <td>使用 <code>/status</code> 和 <code>/debug-config</code> 检查有效设置、策略优先级和受支持字段。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"related-resources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">相关资源</h2> <ul> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">CLI 安装指南</a></p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">受管理的配置</a></p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">Windows 沙箱设置</a></p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b\">Windows 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用</a></p> </li> <li> <p>请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/create-win32-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microsoft Win32 打包指南（需联网）</a></p> </li> <li> <p>请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-win32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microsoft Win32 部署设置（需联网）</a></p> </li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"deploy-the-windows-app-and-codex-cli\">Deploy the Windows app and Codex CLI</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Deploy the Windows desktop app, Codex CLI, or both to managed Windows devices. Choose the app for desktop access or the CLI for terminal access.</p> <p>The desktop app and standalone CLI use different installation contexts. Before deploying the CLI, choose and validate the account used to run its installer.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Your goal</th> <th>Start with</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Distribute the desktop app</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450?anchor=deploy-the-windows-app\">Deploy the Windows app</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Give employees standalone terminal access</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450?anchor=deploy-codex-cli-on-windows\">Deploy Codex CLI on Windows</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Apply Codex requirements on Windows</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450?anchor=configure-managed-requirements\">Configure managed requirements</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Prepare Windows command execution</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450?anchor=configure-the-windows-sandbox\">Configure the Windows sandbox</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"deploy-the-windows-app\">Deploy the Windows app</h2> <p>Choose a method based on your management tool and whether devices can access Microsoft's distribution services.</p> <p>Before deployment, configure applicable controls using <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a>. To prepare Codex command execution in the desktop app, follow <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">Windows sandbox setup</a>. Check device compatibility and complete any required legacy setup.</p> <p>The MSIX links below download the latest release for each architecture, not a historical version. Review the downloaded package and keep the approved artifact in your deployment system. Follow <a href=\"#/article/a-24c62848a3326493\">Manage app updates</a> to coordinate the app's built-in updater with Microsoft Store, Intune, and other deployment tools.</p> <p><a id=\"deploy-the-app-with-an-enterprise-management-tool\"></a></p> <p><strong>windows-deployment</strong></p> <p>Package source</p> <p><strong>windows-intune-source</strong></p> <h3 id=\"deploy-through-microsoft-store\">Deploy through Microsoft Store</h3> <p>Use Intune's Microsoft Store integration to install and update the app.</p> <ol> <li> <p>In the Intune admin center, go to <strong>Apps</strong> &gt; <strong>All apps</strong> &gt; <strong>Create</strong>. Select <strong>Microsoft Store app (new)</strong>.</p> </li> <li> <p>Search for <strong>ChatGPT</strong> from <strong>OpenAI</strong>, or enter the Store product ID <code>9PLM9XGG6VKS</code>. Select the app and review its installation settings.</p> </li> <li> <p>On <strong>App information</strong>, set <strong>Install behavior</strong> to <strong>System</strong>.</p> </li> <li> <p>Under <strong>Required</strong>, add your target group so Intune installs the app automatically, then select <strong>Create</strong>.</p> </li> </ol> <p>For optional installation through Company Portal, use <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong> instead.</p> <p>Devices need access to the Microsoft Store and Windows Update endpoints in Microsoft's <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/fundamentals/endpoints#microsoft-store\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">network requirements (online)</a>. If these endpoints are blocked, select <strong>Offline MSIX</strong>.</p> <p>For installation context, network requirements, and deployment monitoring, see Microsoft's <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-microsoft-store\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Intune Store app guide (online)</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"deploy-an-offline-package-with-intune\">Deploy an offline package with Intune</h3> <p>Use a downloaded MSIX when devices can't use Microsoft's distribution services or you need to distribute a package your organization has reviewed. The links download the latest release. For repeat deployments, use the approved artifact in your deployment system. Choose <strong>Required</strong> for automatic installation.</p> <p>Blocking access to the Microsoft Store app does not prevent deployment through Intune's Microsoft Store integration. You can still use <strong>Microsoft Store (recommended)</strong>.</p> <p>Assignment</p> <p><strong>windows-intune-assignment</strong></p> <ol> <li> <p>Download the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX (online)</a> for your devices.</p> </li> <li> <p>In the Intune admin center, go to <strong>Apps</strong> &gt; <strong>All apps</strong> &gt; <strong>Create</strong>. Select <strong>Line-of-business app</strong>, upload the MSIX, and review the package information.</p> </li> <li> <p>On <strong>Assignments</strong>, add your target device group under <strong>Required</strong>.</p> </li> <li> <p>In that assignment's <strong>Install Context</strong> column, select <strong>User context</strong>, change it to <strong>Device context</strong>, and save.</p> </li> <li> <p>Review and create the app. Confirm successful installation in <strong>Device install status</strong>, then have employees launch ChatGPT normally.</p> </li> </ol> <p>If the app doesn't appear, have users sign out and back in.</p> <p>For more information, see Microsoft's <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-lob-windows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">LOB app deployment guide (online)</a>.</p> <p>To offer installation through Company Portal, deploy the offline package as a <strong>Windows app (Win32)</strong> with an <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong> assignment:</p> <ol> <li> <p>Download the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX (online)</a>, plus the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-License.xml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">offline license (online)</a>. Rename the package to <code>ChatGPT.msix</code> and keep both files in the same folder.</p> </li> <li> <p>Save this script as <code>Install-ChatGPT.ps1</code> beside the downloaded files:</p> </li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">   #Requires -RunAsAdministrator\n   $ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\n   Add-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online `\n     -PackagePath \"$PSScriptRoot\\ChatGPT.msix\" `\n     -LicensePath \"$PSScriptRoot\\ChatGPT-License.xml\" `\n     -Regions all\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Save this script as <code>Uninstall-ChatGPT.ps1</code> beside the MSIX, license, and installation script. Configure Intune to run this script in System context when uninstalling the app. The script removes the provisioned package and app registrations for all users on the device:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">   #Requires -RunAsAdministrator\n   $ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\n   Get-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online |\n     Where-Object DisplayName -eq 'OpenAI.Codex' |\n     Remove-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online -AllUsers\n\n   Get-AppxPackage -AllUsers -Name 'OpenAI.Codex' |\n     Remove-AppxPackage -AllUsers\n</code></pre> <p>Follow your organization's PowerShell script-signing policy for both scripts.</p> <ol> <li>Use Microsoft's <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-win32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Win32 app workflow (online)</a> to package the MSIX, license, <code>Install-ChatGPT.ps1</code>, and <code>Uninstall-ChatGPT.ps1</code> together. Add a <strong>Windows app (Win32)</strong> in Intune, set <strong>Install behavior</strong> to <strong>System</strong>, and target the package's architecture. Configure the 64-bit install and uninstall commands below, then assign the app as <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong>.</li> </ol> <details> <summary>Win32 installation, removal, and detection settings</summary> Set <strong>Install command</strong> to: <pre><code class=\"language-text\">%SystemRoot%\\Sysnative\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe -NoProfile -File .\\Install-ChatGPT.ps1\n</code></pre> For devices where Windows is installed at <code>C:\\Windows</code>, set <strong>Uninstall command</strong> to: <pre><code class=\"language-text\">C:\\Windows\\Sysnative\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe -NoProfile -File .\\Uninstall-ChatGPT.ps1\n</code></pre> Use the actual Windows directory if it differs. This literal path selects 64-bit Windows PowerShell from Intune's 32-bit command context. Do not substitute <code>%SystemRoot%</code> in the uninstall field: Intune does not expand environment variables there. If you need variable expansion, package a wrapper script as described in <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-win32#step-2-program\">Microsoft's program settings (online)</a>. Run this custom detection script in 64-bit PowerShell. It reports success when the app is provisioned on the device. To detect a specific approved version, also compare the package's <code>Version</code> with that version. <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$package = Get-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online -ErrorAction Stop |\n  Where-Object DisplayName -eq 'OpenAI.Codex'\n\nif ($package) {\n  Write-Output $package.PackageName\n  exit 0\n}\nexit 1\n</code></pre> Windows registers the provisioned package at sign-in. If the app doesn't appear, have users sign out and back in. </details> <h3 id=\"deploy-with-microsoft-configuration-manager-sccm\">Deploy with Microsoft Configuration Manager (SCCM)</h3> <p>Deploy the downloaded MSIX through Configuration Manager and Software Center.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Download the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX (online)</a> for your devices. Put it on a network share accessible to Configuration Manager.</p> </li> <li> <p>Go to <strong>Software Library</strong> &gt; <strong>Application Management</strong> &gt; <strong>Applications</strong> &gt; <strong>Create Application</strong>. Select <strong>Windows app package</strong> and enter the MSIX path. Review the detected package information and enable <strong>Provision this application for all users on the device</strong>.</p> </li> <li> <p>Distribute the content to your distribution points and deploy to a device collection. Choose <strong>Required</strong> to install automatically, or <strong>Available</strong> to let users install from Software Center.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Use the Windows app package deployment type, not the Store-link type. See Microsoft's <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/configmgr/apps/get-started/creating-windows-applications\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Configuration Manager guide (online)</a> for package requirements and all-user provisioning.</p> <p>If your deployment workflow requires it, download the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-License.xml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">offline license (online)</a> alongside the package.</p> <h4 id=\"remove-a-provisioned-app-with-configuration-manager\">Remove a provisioned app with Configuration Manager</h4> <p>If users have already signed in to devices with the provisioned app, create both uninstall deployments:</p> <ol> <li> <p>Target an uninstall deployment to the <strong>device collection</strong> containing the affected devices.</p> </li> <li> <p>Target a second uninstall deployment to the <strong>user collection</strong> containing users who have already signed in to those devices.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Removing the provisioned app from the device does not uninstall it for existing users. Verify removal for both the device and those user accounts. See Microsoft's <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/configmgr/apps/get-started/creating-windows-applications#provision-windows-app-packages-for-all-users-on-a-device\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">provisioned app removal guidance (online)</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"deploy-with-another-management-tool\">Deploy with another management tool</h3> <p>Use your management tool's MSIX deployment workflow.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Download the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX (online)</a> for your devices.</p> </li> <li> <p>Add the MSIX to your deployment tool. Configure installation for the device, using Local System or administrator privileges.</p> </li> <li> <p>Assign automatic installation to a pilot device group. Confirm that employees can open ChatGPT under their normal Windows accounts before expanding deployment.</p> </li> </ol> <p>If the app doesn't appear, have users sign out and back in.</p> <details> <summary>Install with a PowerShell script</summary> If your tool requires an installation command, download the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-License.xml\">offline license (online)</a> alongside the MSIX. Rename the package to <code>ChatGPT.msix</code> and save this script as <code>Install-ChatGPT.ps1</code> in the same folder: <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">#Requires -RunAsAdministrator\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'\n\nAdd-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online `\n  -PackagePath \"$PSScriptRoot\\ChatGPT.msix\" `\n  -LicensePath \"$PSScriptRoot\\ChatGPT-License.xml\" `\n  -Regions all\n</code></pre> Package the script and both files together. Configure your tool to run the script with 64-bit Windows PowerShell as Local System or an administrator. </details> <p><a id=\"let-users-install-and-update-the-app\"></a></p> <p>Package source</p> <p><strong>windows-user-source</strong></p> <h3 id=\"let-users-install-the-app\">Let users install the app</h3> <p>Use this option when users can install applications themselves or get help from an administrator.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Direct users to the <a href=\"https://get.microsoft.com/installer/download/9PLM9XGG6VKS?cid=website_cta_psi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Windows installer (online)</a>.</p> </li> <li> <p>Run the installer and follow the Windows installation prompts. An administrator must approve the installation.</p> </li> <li> <p>Open ChatGPT and sign in with a work account.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Users can also install from the command line:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">winget install --id 9PLM9XGG6VKS -s msstore\n</code></pre> <p>The installer provides automatic updates. Microsoft Store components may appear during installation or updates; users don't need to browse the Store.</p> <p><a id=\"install-without-microsoft-distribution-services\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"install-from-an-offline-package\">Install from an offline package</h3> <p>Download the files on a connected machine, then copy them to the target device. An administrator must perform the installation.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Download the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-x64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">x64 MSIX (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-arm64.msix\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Arm64 MSIX (online)</a>, plus the <a href=\"https://persistent.oaistatic.com/codex-app-prod/ChatGPT-License.xml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">offline license (online)</a>. Rename the package to <code>ChatGPT.msix</code> and keep both files in the same folder.</p> </li> <li> <p>Open Windows PowerShell as an administrator in that folder and run:</p> </li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">   Add-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online `\n     -PackagePath .\\ChatGPT.msix `\n     -LicensePath .\\ChatGPT-License.xml `\n     -Regions all\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Sign out and back in if the app doesn't appear, then open ChatGPT and sign in with a work account.</li> </ol> <p>The download links provide the latest Store-signed package for each architecture. Offline installation still requires online access to use ChatGPT. Standalone MSI and non-Store EXE packages aren't available for the desktop app.</p> <h2 id=\"deploy-codex-cli-on-windows\">Deploy Codex CLI on Windows</h2> <p>Prepare the CLI package, apply your device policy, and verify terminal access from the employee's account.</p> <h3 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h3> <ul> <li> <p>Identify the target Windows devices and users and their processor architectures, then choose an installation method. Confirm that users have Codex access and can complete your organization's sign-in flow.</p> </li> <li> <p>For Intune, prepare app-management permissions, enrolled devices that meet <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/create-win32-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microsoft's Win32 packaging prerequisites (online)</a>, and an unattended installation package.</p> </li> <li> <p>Assign responsibility for CLI updates and removal. If you use npm, account for the managed Node.js/npm installation and its global package location.</p> </li> </ul> <h3 id=\"choose-an-installation-method\">Choose an installation method</h3> <p>Choose an installation method and an explicit CLI release. Review the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI releases on GitHub (online)</a>, then replace <code>&lt;approved-version&gt;</code> in the examples with your approved version number in <code>x.y.z</code> form. Use the same version in your package and detection rule.</p> <p>The standalone installer defaults to <code>latest</code> when no release is specified. Set <code>-Release</code> explicitly to pin the deployment to a release; see the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d/scripts/install/install.ps1#L1-L14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">installer's release parameter (online)</a>. For general installation guidance, see <a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">CLI installation</a>.</p> <p><strong>Standalone PowerShell installer.</strong> From a new PowerShell window, download the installer and pass the approved release:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$CodexRelease = '&lt;approved-version&gt;'\nInvoke-WebRequest -UseBasicParsing -Uri 'https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1' -OutFile '.\\codex-install.ps1'\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\codex-install.ps1 -Release $CodexRelease\n</code></pre> <p><strong>npm.</strong> If Node.js and npm are already managed on the device, select the approved package version explicitly:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$CodexRelease = '&lt;approved-version&gt;'\nnpm install -g \"@openai/codex@$CodexRelease\"\n</code></pre> <p>For managed distribution, keep the reviewed installer or package artifact and selected release in your IT-owned package. Define installation context, detection, removal, and update behavior. Selecting a version does not change the installer's user-profile defaults or provide a complete unattended deployment wrapper.</p> <h3 id=\"set-the-installation-context\">Set the installation context</h3> <p>The <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">standalone installer (online)</a> defaults to runtime files in the current user's profile, a command directory at <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\OpenAI\\Codex\\bin</code>, and the <strong>User PATH</strong>.</p> <p>Running the unchanged installer as <strong>SYSTEM</strong> targets the SYSTEM profile and environment. Selecting <strong>System</strong> in Intune does not make this an all-users installation.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Deployment choice</th> <th>What to validate</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Install for the signed-in employee</td> <td>Run installation and detection in that user's context. Open a new terminal and confirm that the employee can resolve and run <code>codex</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Build a device-wide package</td> <td>Define and validate the machine installation layout, runtime files, permissions, PATH exposure, detection, and removal. The default installer does not provide this design.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Use npm</td> <td>Confirm the global package prefix and command location for the account running npm. “Global” does not necessarily mean all Windows users.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Separate user installation, device policy delivery, and administrator-approved sandbox setup. When a procedure requires an employee's profile, use that employee's identity rather than SYSTEM.</p> <p>Keep the standalone runtime files together; copying only <code>codex.exe</code> is not a complete standalone package.</p> <h3 id=\"package-and-assign-the-cli-through-intune\">Package and assign the CLI through Intune</h3> <p>Prepare and validate an IT-owned Win32 package with an unattended installer, uninstaller, and detection logic for the chosen installation context.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Prepare a source folder containing the approved installation payload and your unattended setup script. Specify the approved CLI release in that script rather than allowing it to resolve <code>latest</code>. Keep the Microsoft packaging tool and output folder outside that source folder.</p> </li> <li> <p>Generate the <code>.intunewin</code> file with the Microsoft Win32 Content Prep Tool. This example assumes your reviewed setup script is named <code>Install-Codex.ps1</code>:</p> </li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">   IntuneWinAppUtil.exe -c C:\\Packages\\Codex\\Source -s Install-Codex.ps1 -o C:\\Packages\\Codex\\Output -q\n</code></pre> <p>The tool packages the source folder's contents. See <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/create-win32-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Create a Win32 app package (online)</a>.</p> <ol> <li> <p>In Intune, create a <strong>Windows app (Win32)</strong> and upload the package.</p> </li> <li> <p>Set the install and uninstall commands, <strong>User</strong> or <strong>System</strong> behavior, requirements, and detection rules to match the package.</p> </li> <li> <p>Assign it as <strong>Required</strong> or <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong>.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Intune requires unattended installation. Custom detection scripts must exit with code <code>0</code> and write to stdout; output on stderr causes detection failure. See <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-win32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add and assign a Win32 app (online)</a>.</p> <p>Verify the CLI from the employee's account, even when the management agent reports a successful exit code.</p> <p>For Configuration Manager (SCCM), use the reviewed CLI installation design in your application workflow, with a CLI-specific installer and detection rule. The desktop app's MSIX settings apply only to the desktop app.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-managed-requirements\">Configure managed requirements</h3> <p>Deploy administrator-enforced Windows requirements to:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">%ProgramData%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\requirements.toml\n</code></pre> <p>Deliver the file through your endpoint management tool. Give intended users read access and prevent ordinary users from changing the administrator-owned policy.</p> <p>Requirements constrain settings; configuration defaults supply starting values. Review both the local file and applicable cloud policy to determine the effective configuration.</p> <p>Choose requirements for permissions, approvals, network access, and sandbox behavior. See <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=locations-and-precedence\">Managed configuration</a> for supported fields and precedence.</p> <p>After deployment, launch Codex as the employee and use <code>/status</code> and <code>/debug-config</code> to confirm the effective policy. Installing the CLI or delivering requirements does not grant workspace access.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-the-windows-sandbox\">Configure the Windows sandbox</h3> <p>Check device compatibility before choosing a Windows sandbox. The <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">Windows sandbox guide</a> covers Microsoft Execution Containers (MXC) and the legacy implementations.</p> <h4 id=\"prefer-mxc-on-compatible-devices\">Prefer MXC on compatible devices</h4> <p>For standalone CLI use, enable MXC preference in <code>config.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[features]\nprefer_mxc = true\n</code></pre> <p>You can also enforce this feature value through <code>requirements.toml</code>. The preference permits legacy fallback when MXC is unavailable. Check the device requirements in the Windows sandbox guide before enabling it.</p> <p>On CLI version 0.162.0 or later, run this compatibility probe from a project directory:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">codex -c windows.sandbox=mxc sandbox --include-managed-config --permission-profile :workspace -- cmd.exe /d /c echo MXC_OK\n$LASTEXITCODE\n</code></pre> <p>Expect <code>MXC_OK</code> and an exit code of <code>0</code>. This checks the explicit MXC command; also inspect the employee's normal session configuration.</p> <p>Before rollout, compare the sandbox guide's networking constraints with your managed network policy.</p> <h4 id=\"prepare-the-legacy-fallback\">Prepare the legacy fallback</h4> <p>When MXC is unavailable or disabled, prefer the <code>elevated</code> legacy fallback. It requires administrator-approved setup, but sandboxed commands run without administrator privileges.</p> <p>Follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">IT-led setup procedure</a> for the employee account and Codex home. Run this example from an appropriately elevated process:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">codex sandbox setup --elevated --user 'DOMAIN\\alice' --codex-home 'C:\\Users\\alice\\.codex'\n</code></pre> <p>Replace the sample identity and path with the intended user's values. Use an administrator-trusted CLI installation for elevated setup.</p> <p>To permit only the elevated legacy implementation, add the following to <code>%ProgramData%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\requirements.toml</code>, not <code>config.toml</code>. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2?anchor=configure-a-legacy-fallback\">Configure a legacy fallback</a>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[windows]\nallowed_sandbox_implementations = [\"elevated\"]\n</code></pre> <p>This restricts legacy fallback without blocking MXC. Before allowing <code>unelevated</code>, review its weaker network isolation and lack of denied-read-path support.</p> <h3 id=\"verify-cli-deployment\">Verify CLI deployment</h3> <p>As an intended employee, open a new PowerShell window without administrator privileges:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">Get-Command codex\ncodex --version\ncodex\n</code></pre> <p>Confirm that the executable resolves to the intended installation, then complete the approved sign-in flow. Run a small task in a designated test project and inspect the active configuration.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Check</th> <th>Action and expected result</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Installation context</td> <td>Confirm that the CLI resolves from the intended employee's account, including after a new sign-in.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Management-tool detection</td> <td>Check that devices with the CLI installed are detected and that devices without it, including devices where it was removed, are not detected.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Managed requirements</td> <td>Confirm that the session shows the expected effective policy.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Windows sandbox</td> <td>Verify that MXC works on compatible devices and the approved legacy fallback is provisioned where required.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Update</td> <td>Confirm that the employee can run the approved new version after deployment.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Removal</td> <td>Confirm that the package removes its installation and PATH entry without deleting unrelated user configuration or project data.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"manage-in-app-updates\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"manage-updates\">Manage updates</h2> <h3 id=\"desktop-app\">Desktop app</h3> <p>The app checks for updates by default, including after an offline installation. To enable automatic updates, allow devices to reach <code>persistent.oaistatic.com</code>. If you disable automatic updates, deploy newer packages through your management tool.</p> <p>Follow <a href=\"#/article/a-24c62848a3326493\">Manage app updates</a> to coordinate all update sources. Disabling the built-in updater does not stop Microsoft Store, Intune, or other management tools from updating the app, nor does it provide OpenAI-managed version pinning or a separate release channel. Confirm the installed version through your deployment system.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-cli\">Codex CLI</h3> <p>For each CLI update, choose a new approved release, update the explicit <code>-Release</code> value or npm package version in your deployment package, and update its detection rule. Deploy through your package process, then verify the installed version, account context, and detection behavior. Do not switch the managed package back to an installer command without an explicit release. See <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI releases (online)</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">CLI installation and updates</a>, and <a href=\"https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/using-npm/package-spec\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">npm version selection (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h2> <details> <summary>Users are prompted for administrator credentials when installing</summary> When users install the app themselves, an administrator must approve the installation. For an Intune deployment through the Microsoft Store: 1. In the Intune admin center, go to <strong>Apps</strong> &gt; <strong>All apps</strong> and select ChatGPT. 2. Check <strong>Install behavior</strong> in the app's <strong>Properties</strong>. If it's <strong>User</strong>, add the app again as a <strong>Microsoft Store app (new)</strong> and select <strong>System</strong> on <strong>App information</strong>. 3. Assign the app to your target group under <strong>Required</strong> or <strong>Available for enrolled devices</strong>. If you added a new app, remove that group's assignment from the original app. 4. Sync the affected device with Intune, then check <strong>Device install status</strong>. For an available assignment, retry the installation in Company Portal. If the app is already installed, deploying it with <strong>System</strong> install behavior may cause Intune to report <code>0x87D1041C</code>. Installation still succeeds in this scenario. Verify the app on the affected device. </details> <details> <summary>Installation fails with error <code>0x80073D28</code></summary> Windows returns <code>0x80073D28</code> (<code>ERROR_PACKAGED_SERVICE_REQUIRES_ADMIN_PRIVILEGES</code>) when it can't install a packaged service without administrator privileges. Run the installation as an administrator, or configure your deployment tool to install in device or System context. For an existing SCCM deployment: 1. Open the application's <strong>Properties</strong> &gt; <strong>Deployment Types</strong>. 2. Edit the <strong>Windows app package</strong> deployment type and open <strong>User Experience</strong>. 3. Enable <strong>Provision this application for all users on the device</strong> and save. 4. Refresh the client's machine policy, then retry the installation in Software Center. For details about the provisioning setting, see Microsoft's <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/configmgr/apps/deploy-use/create-applications#automatically-detect-application-information\">application deployment settings (online)</a>. </details> <h3 id=\"codex-cli-installation-and-configuration\">Codex CLI installation and configuration</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Symptom</th> <th>What to check</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Intune reports success, but the employee cannot run Codex</td> <td>Check the installation account, runtime location, and account whose PATH was updated. The unchanged installer running as SYSTEM does not install into the employee's profile.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>codex</code> is not recognized after installation</td> <td>Open a new terminal. Check the intended account's command directory and PATH.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>The wrong Codex version starts</td> <td>Use <code>Get-Command codex</code> to check for competing standalone or npm locations.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>MXC probe fails</td> <td>Check device capabilities, CLI version, and managed policy against the Windows sandbox guide. Provision the approved legacy fallback where appropriate.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Legacy sandbox setup requests administrator approval</td> <td>Complete IT-led setup for the employee's identity and Codex home.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Managed settings differ from the local requirements file</td> <td>Use <code>/status</code> and <code>/debug-config</code> to review effective settings, policy precedence, and supported fields.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"related-resources\">Related resources</h2> <ul> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">CLI installation</a></p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a></p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">Windows sandbox setup</a></p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b\">ChatGPT desktop app for Windows</a></p> </li> <li> <p>See <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/create-win32-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microsoft Win32 packaging guide (online)</a></p> </li> <li> <p>See <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/app-management/deployment/add-win32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Microsoft Win32 deployment settings (online)</a></p> </li> </ul>"};
